spaceknife run <命令序列>\n\n按顺序执行与 SpaceSni:
spaceknife run <commands>

Runs the same commands as SpaceSniffer, in order, without opening a window. The whole sequence is checked first; if anything is wrong, nothing runs.

  help                          Show this help
  scan "<path>"                 Scan a folder or disk and open a view; separate several paths with ; (one view)
  load "<snapshot>"             Open a SpaceKnife snapshot (.sks) as a view
  filter "<expression>"         Filter the previous view (syntax: docs/filter-syntax.md)
  save "<file>"                 Save the full result of the previous view as a snapshot (the filter doesn't apply)
  export "<template>" "<file>"  Export the previous view to a file (the filtered content); <template> is a built-in
                                template name, csv / json / html, or the path of a template file
                                (syntax: docs/export-templates.md)
  autoclose                     Don't show the view summaries at the end

Meta commands (each must be a single word without delimiters):
  @delim=X  @delim=XY           Use X as the delimiter of the parameters that follow (or X to open and Y to close);
                                the default is "
  @parser=OS                    Parse everything again from the start with the arguments as the system split them;
                                no meta commands are accepted after it

Built-in templates: {builtins}
Export formats: {formats}

Example: spaceknife run scan "D:\Photos" filter "*.jpg;>5mb" export "Simple file list" big.txt autoclose
